{"slug": "kimi-k3", "names": ["Kimi K3"], "data": {"data": [{"author_id": "498492725", "created_at": "2026-09-27T15:36:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2104233812909822133"], "id": "2104233812909822133", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4428, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "WHY KIMI K3 AND K2.6 ARE EXCELLING IN LONG-CONTEXT REASONING\n\nKimi models have earned a stellar reputation across the global AI developer community for their exceptional long-context comprehension and retrieval accuracy.\n\nWith https://t.co/SBrDSky0eM Responses API adding official https://t.co/5C39xZHoe8", "url": "https://x.com/Happy_hillman/status/2104233812909822133"}, {"author_id": "2090161486291169281", "created_at": "2026-09-27T10:54:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2104162807130284408"], "id": "2104162807130284408", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2103117290044600525", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "CHINA JUST DESTROYED CLAUDE AI AND IT\u2019S 100% FREE.\n\nA developer revealed how Moonshot AI open-weights Kimi K3 outperforms closed models like Claude Opus while costing $0 on open source.\n\nThe clip showed Kimi K3 building complex 3D interactive physics environments, FPS game https://t.co/Ze946PnYLx https://t.co/2qXwigv3qu", "url": "https://x.com/pavel_go000/status/2104162807130284408"}, {"author_id": "2030516877748002816", "created_at": "2026-10-07T18:12:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2107896908908011783"], "id": "2107896908908011783", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 52, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\ud83d\udea8 KIMI K3 JUST CRASHED THE FRONTIER AI PARTY.\n\nFor years, frontier AI lived behind closed doors.\n\nOpenAI. Anthropic. Google.\n\nYou could use their models \u2014 but you didn't own the weights.\n\nThen came Kimi K3. \ud83d\udc40\n\n\ud83d\udd25 2.8 TRILLION parameters\n\ud83e\udde0 ~104B active parameters\n\u26a1 896 MoE https://t.co/yfMpohd1lg", "url": "https://x.com/_yadav1825_/status/2107896908908011783"}, {"author_id": "1809111977387831296", "created_at": "2026-09-16T11:26:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100184534234874172"], "id": "2100184534234874172", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1809111977387831296", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2100184336733540530", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_ak_111 For refactoring kimi k3 is better but you can use astra but you need 200$ plan for that the 100$ or 20$ plan not Worth it", "url": "https://x.com/mohamed_yo32851/status/2100184534234874172"}, {"author_id": "498492725", "created_at": "2026-09-27T15:22:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2104230239010492447"], "id": "2104230239010492447", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9936, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "KIMI AND GLM JOIN THE PARTY: EXPANDING YOUR CODEX TOOLKIT\n\nFor developers relying heavily on Codex for daily software development, having access to diverse reasoning models inside your local environment is the ultimate superpower. Different model families possess unique https://t.co/NMqGcYwkGg", "url": "https://x.com/Happy_hillman/status/2104230239010492447"}, {"author_id": "2058490812363575296", "created_at": "2026-09-24T07:00:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103016741916037235"], "id": "2103016741916037235", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4485, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2102029865675551172", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "\ud83d\ude80 PROGRAMMING &amp; AGENT SPECIALIST: MOONSHOT AI\u2019S KIMI K2.8 PREVIEW ARRIVES ON https://t.co/fEDs0n3D2S! \u26a1\ud83c\udf19\ud83e\udde0\ud83c\udf10\n\nA dedicated evolution for software developers, autonomous agents, and multi-file codebases has landed on the https://t.co/fEDs0n3D2S API grid and Web Chat! Developed https://t.co/Lym7fIvDr8 https://t.co/wvQ3yTsZri", "url": "https://x.com/ORACLE_OKLA/status/2103016741916037235"}, {"author_id": "2074922171647078400", "created_at": "2026-10-14T01:10:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110176396928835635"], "id": "2110176396928835635", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Muse Wonder (Max) lands at WebDev #15 with 1651 points \u2014 just 4 points behind Kimi K3 (Max). Caveat: Arena ranking doesn't measure real-world project complexity or debugging depth. [s1]", "url": "https://x.com/kelceykinn/status/2110176396928835635"}, {"author_id": "2101905162910797824", "created_at": "2026-09-22T05:14:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2102265333088428242"], "id": "2102265333088428242", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Need a massive refactoring script but don't want to hit a 128k context limit? \ud83d\udcbb\n\nWe asked Kimi K3 (Moonshot\u2019s massive 2.8T model built specifically for hard coding) to rewrite a legacy Python codebase. Nailed the architecture in seconds.\nNo login. 1M context window. Just code.", "url": "https://x.com/UsingOpen/status/2102265333088428242"}, {"author_id": "2788825408", "created_at": "2026-09-24T14:09:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103124709852197268", "2103125257272066305"], "id": "2103124709852197268", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Rankings crown Claude king.\nBuilders know better.\n\n- OpenAI: GPT-6 Astra\n- Anthropic: Claude Opus 5.5\n- Moonshot: Kimi K3\n- xAI: Grok 4.7\n- ZAI: GLM 5.3\n\nGrok 4.7 cut my refactor time in half last month. Which model broke on your last production task? https://t.co/1ckRrqxVqp", "url": "https://x.com/andrydina7/status/2103124709852197268"}, {"author_id": "2788825408", "created_at": "2026-09-24T14:11:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103124709852197268", "2103125257272066305"], "id": "2103125257272066305", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Rankings crown Claude king.\nBuilders know better.\n\n- OpenAI: GPT-6 Astra\n- Anthropic: Claude Opus 5.5\n- Moonshot: Kimi K3\n- xAI: Grok 4.7\n- ZAI: GLM 5.3\n\nGrok 4.7 cut my refactor time in half last month. Which model broke on your last production task? https://t.co/wZeG9SQJXX", "url": "https://x.com/andrydina7/status/2103125257272066305"}, {"author_id": "1160898451044880384", "created_at": "2026-09-16T17:14:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100272224876007782"], "id": "2100272224876007782", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 79, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kritikakodes - Claude Pro -&gt; primary\n- Antigravity + Pro Subscription -&gt; secondary + web search\n- ChatGPT Pro -&gt; testing codex and 5.6 sol models but using its Go plan for research\n- Kimi K3 -&gt; for debugging\n- Qwen 5.3 -&gt; AI tools that I am working on", "url": "https://x.com/solitrix02/status/2100272224876007782"}, {"author_id": "1809111977387831296", "created_at": "2026-09-16T11:25:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100184336733540530"], "id": "2100184336733540530", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2042826624488349696", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 52, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2099903084231356918", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_ak_111 Deepseek v4.1 flash for build and kimi k3 for planing and glm 5.3 max for improving the security stuff in the plan and add more secure code letter that all you need and maybe maybe maaaaybe gpt 5.6 sol for review the code after finishing the product and refactor this at the end", "url": "https://x.com/mohamed_yo32851/status/2100184336733540530"}, {"author_id": "1258455699073441793", "created_at": "2026-09-16T09:52:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100160860752605650"], "id": "2100160860752605650", "in_reply_to_user_id": "838729515069222912", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 76, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2100112122596167940", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@mahlatsemariba hey man so i orchestrate with Astra on codex, it handles the planning, debugging and reviews, factory droid is my execution harness , GLM 5.3 is my daily worker, Gemini 3.8 flash does frontend/UI/UX, Kimi K3 the chief, then Hermes + DeepSeek V4.1 flash for research....", "url": "https://x.com/Lukhanyo_19/status/2100160860752605650"}, {"author_id": "1777080448365047808", "created_at": "2026-10-03T14:45:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106395193725342118"], "id": "2106395193725342118", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1778842279442055168", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2106366933633319163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@blueemi99 The benchmark war is going meta: the White House accuses Moonshot of distilling Anthropic's Fable into Kimi K3. \"Better at debugging\" might just mean \"better at copying.\"", "url": "https://x.com/SumarryHQ/status/2106395193725342118"}, {"author_id": "1682428283135336449", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2109131880977072150"], "id": "2109131880977072150", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 134, "impression_count": 9495, "like_count": 147, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Kimi K3 is a 2.8-trillion-parameter model.\nSomeone is distilled its coding-agent behavior into Qwen3.5-9B and the Q4 GGUF is 5.9GB.\n\nNot Kimi's 2.8T parameters but its behavior.\n\nThe training set captures 582 real Kimi K3 agent trajectories:\n\ud83d\udd0e inspect repos\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f call tools\n\ud83e\uddea run https://t.co/2VLu8vrx5N", "url": "https://x.com/TeksEdge/status/2109131880977072150"}, {"author_id": "1130838006770864128", "created_at": "2026-10-13T14:17:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2110012119974576335"], "id": "2110012119974576335", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2370091", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2109994351418114147", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@scottkeckwarren Nice trick with the scheduled Hi. For the refactor hours themselves, you could point Claude Code at CodeFast's unlimited Kimi K3 (50 TRY for 24 hours) and keep the Claude window for the parts that really need it: https://t.co/00YY7prOlU", "url": "https://x.com/vibecoderpromax/status/2110012119974576335"}, {"author_id": "1797693526936829952", "created_at": "2026-09-21T20:09:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2102128090511982839"], "id": "2102128090511982839", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18391, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\ud835\uddde\ud835\udddc\ud835\udde0\ud835\udddc \ud835\uddde\ud835\udfee.\ud835\udff4 \ud835\udde3\ud835\udde5\ud835\uddd8\ud835\udde9\ud835\udddc\ud835\uddd8\ud835\uddea \ud835\udddc\ud835\udde6 \ud835\udde1\ud835\udde2\ud835\uddea \ud835\udddf\ud835\udddc\ud835\udde9\ud835\uddd8 \ud835\udde2\ud835\udde1 \ud835\uddd5.\ud835\uddd4\ud835\udddc\n\nhttps://t.co/wTkAmx5NfA is expanding its model lineup with Kimi K2.8 Preview, Moonshot AI\u2019s latest model built specifically for coding and agent-driven workflows.\n\nWhat makes this release notable?\n\n\ud83e\udde0 1M+ TOKEN https://t.co/1gR1UnGXKV", "url": "https://x.com/skyprince70/status/2102128090511982839"}, {"author_id": "1903022486603583488", "created_at": "2026-09-21T06:34:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2101923124010795062"], "id": "2101923124010795062", "in_reply_to_user_id": "23113993", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 119, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2101873007673086304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@minchoi Realtime Research \u2192 GPT 5.6 sol\nPlanning &amp; Orchestration\u2192 Fable 5.1\nDay-to-day Coding/Debug \u2192 Deepseek V4.1 flash/GLM 5.3 flash\nWrite &amp; Run Tests \u2192 DeepSeek V4.1 Flash/GLM 5.3 Flash\nComplex Coding/Debug \u2192 GPT 5.6 sol/GPT-6 Astra/Fable 5.1\nFrontend \u2192 Fable 5.1/Kimi K3", "url": "https://x.com/HydratedViper_/status/2101923124010795062"}, {"author_id": "2101905162910797824", "created_at": "2026-10-03T03:38:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106227263260020971"], "id": "2106227263260020971", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"Vibe coding\" is great, but enterprise refactoring requires a heavyweight. \ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f\n\nWe fed a 10,000-line legacy Python monolith to Kimi K3 (Moonshot\u2019s 2.8T coding beast). It didn't just format the code; it identified circular dependencies, suggested microservice boundaries, and wrote", "url": "https://x.com/UsingOpen/status/2106227263260020971"}, {"author_id": "962314221211062273", "created_at": "2026-09-16T14:01:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100223450757415358"], "id": "2100223450757415358", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 102, "impression_count": 10905, "like_count": 125, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 16}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2098714638552559806", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "GPT-6 Astra + Kimi K3 can still fail as a system if the router keeps sending work to the wrong brain\n\nthe formula: Reliable Routing = Failure Patterns + Rules + Small Judge + Handoff Contract + Measurement\n\n7% -&gt; FIND: study failed tasks before writing routing rules. separate https://t.co/czzhx8i2M4 https://t.co/n2j2wgyh8O", "url": "https://x.com/de1lymoon/status/2100223450757415358"}, {"author_id": "11373922", "created_at": "2026-10-10T17:08:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2108967809518572022"], "id": "2108967809518572022", "in_reply_to_user_id": "59268061", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 34, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2108834533466329279", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@xonecas It must be some very strange interaction in my Researcher agent, which has a custom prompt. Kimi K3 exhibited the same \"hmm\" and looped in the same way. Switching to the built-in Plan agent worked.\n\nHow do you even begin to debug this? \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f", "url": "https://x.com/ampajaro/status/2108967809518572022"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"article": {"title": "The Kimi k3 Breakthrough: How Next-Gen AI Reasoning Is Giving Virtual Companions a Soul?"}, "author_id": "2090161486291169281", "created_at": "2026-09-24T13:40:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2103117290044600525"], "id": "2103117290044600525", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 885, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/l5PLqv3sP3"}, {"author_id": "1809111977387831296", "created_at": "2026-09-16T11:25:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100184336733540530"], "id": "2100184336733540530", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2042826624488349696", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 52, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2099903084231356918", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@_ak_111 Deepseek v4.1 flash for build and kimi k3 for planing and glm 5.3 max for improving the security stuff in the plan and add more secure code letter that all you need and maybe maybe maaaaybe gpt 5.6 sol for review the code after finishing the product and refactor this at the end"}, {"author_id": "1392094167522742272", "created_at": "2026-09-21T13:39:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2102029865675551172"], "id": "2102029865675551172", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 8031, "like_count": 36, "quote_count": 13, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "\ud83d\udce2 Kimi K2.8 Preview \u73b0\u5df2\u767b\u9646 https://t.co/Yl2KG97Eb1\n\n\u4f5c\u4e3a Moonshot AI \u4e13\u4e3a\u7f16\u7a0b\u4e0e Agent \u5de5\u4f5c\u6d41\u6253\u9020\u7684\u6700\u65b0\u9884\u89c8\u6a21\u578b\uff0cKimi K2.8 Preview \u652f\u6301 1M (1,048,576 Token) \u8d85\u957f\u4e0a\u4e0b\u6587\u4e0e\u6587\u672c/\u56fe\u7247/\u89c6\u9891\u591a\u6a21\u6001\u8f93\u5165\u3002\u5176\u7efc\u5408\u6027\u80fd\u76f4\u903c Kimi K3\uff0c\u76f8\u6bd4 K2.7 Code \u5177\u5907\u66f4\u9ad8\u6548\u7684\u601d\u8003\u4e0e\u4ee3\u7801\u80fd\u529b\uff0c\u5e76\u652f\u6301 https://t.co/1XRb5WC0zF"}, {"author_id": "2042826624488349696", "created_at": "2026-09-15T16:48:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2099903084231356918"], "id": "2099903084231356918", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 9874, "like_count": 48, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 72, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "be honest\u2026 which Chinese AI model would you trust to build a serious app?"}, {"author_id": "838729515069222912", "created_at": "2026-09-16T06:38:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2100112122596167940"], "id": "2100112122596167940", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1258455699073441793", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 35, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2100077641973858675", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Lukhanyo_19 How are you using deepseek bro? I haven\u2019t explored open source models with building. Just been using Claude and codex"}, {"author_id": "1778842279442055168", "created_at": "2026-10-03T12:53:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2106366933633319163"], "id": "2106366933633319163", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 17, "impression_count": 19949, "like_count": 162, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 52, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Burning hot take: Opus 5.5 isnt THAT good for plain code quality and debugging.\n\nEvery benchmark shows it by far above, and i agree. Overall it is a much better model than anything else, but for plain debugging, Astra and Fable (even old 5.1) are a lot better, probably just"}, {"author_id": "2370091", "created_at": "2026-10-13T13:07:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2109994351418114147"], "id": "2109994351418114147", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 98, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My Claude Code limit kept running out at 11 AM with a 3 PM reset, right in the middle of a refactor.\n\nThe 5-hour window starts with your first message. Now a scheduled \"Hi\" goes out before I start work, and the reset lands at lunch.\n\n#ClaudeCode #AI #DevProductivity https://t.co/MN2ZMT3TKp"}, {"author_id": "23113993", "created_at": "2026-09-21T03:15:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2101873007673086304"], "id": "2101873007673086304", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5642, "impression_count": 7906028, "like_count": 3215, "quote_count": 66, "reply_count": 357, "retweet_count": 206}, "text": "This is literally my new workflow now:\n\nRealtime Research \u2192 Grok Bot\nPlanning &amp; Orchestration\u2192 Grok Bot\nDay-to-day Coding/Debug \u2192 Grok Build + Grok 4.6\nWri